# mobile.rules
# Cross-platform mobile code (e.g. React Native/Flutter shared layer). Platform-specific
# native code is also covered by ios.rules or android.rules where applicable.
version: 1

## MUST
- No hardcoded API URLs, hostnames, or environment-specific values; use the environment config module.
- No secrets, API keys, or signing credentials committed to the repo.
- Network calls handle offline/timeout/error states explicitly; no silent failures.

## SHOULD
- New screens/flows are covered by at least one UI or snapshot test.
- Expensive operations (image processing, large lists) are kept off the main/UI thread.

## SECURITY
- Sensitive data (tokens, PII) is stored using secure/encrypted storage, not plain shared preferences/UserDefaults or plain files.
- Deep links and intent filters validate their input before acting on it.

## ARCHITECTURE
- Shared logic between platforms lives in the shared/common module, not duplicated per-platform.
